INSERT INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES
('overlord-sindel', 'Overlord Sindel', 'Sin''Jii Sagshupah (true name)', 'Deevil Overlord, leader of the Steel Bloods army', 'rifts', 'Beast (Greater Deevil of Dyval)', '12th level; no O.C.C. is printed (as printed)', 12, 'Diabolic', 'Effectively Immortal', '18 feet (5.5 m)', 'Three tons, rising to five tons in his steel form', '{"IQ":17,"ME":20,"MA":20,"PS":34,"PP":20,"PE":22,"PB":14,"Spd":28}', 200, 152, 484, 422, NULL, 15, 15, '{"attacks":9,"initiative":2,"strike":9,"parry":7,"dodge":7,"pull":6,"roll":4}', 'Spd 28 running and 110 flying (75 mph/120 km). In his steel form P.S. becomes 54, running Spd falls to 14, M.D.C. rises to 1,284 (800 more) and Horror Factor to 17. Hit Points 200, S.D.C. 152 and A.R. 15 are the block''s S.D.C.-setting figures; in steel those become 852 S.D.C. and A.R. 17. Also +10 to save vs Horror Factor, +7 vs magic, +6 vs psionics and +3 on Perception. Supernatural P.S. 34. W.P. Archery, W.P. Axe, W.P. Energy Rifle, W.P. Pole Arm, W.P. Spear and Paired Weapons.', '[{"name":"Animal Husbandry","pct":96},{"name":"Anthropology","pct":98},{"name":"Barter","pct":98},{"name":"Climbing","pct":98},{"name":"Detect Ambush","pct":98},{"name":"Detect Concealment","pct":93},{"name":"Dowsing","pct":98},{"name":"Horsemanship: Exotic Animals","pct":98},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":89},{"name":"Interrogation","pct":93},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Literacy: Dragonese/Elven","pct":96},{"name":"Literacy: American","pct":96},{"name":"Lore: Demons & Monsters","pct":98},{"name":"Mathematics: Basic","pct":96},{"name":"Military Etiquette","pct":96},{"name":"Military Fortification","pct":88},{"name":"Play Musical Instrument","pct":75},{"name":"Hover Craft (ground)","pct":98},{"name":"Prowl","pct":83},{"name":"Recognize Weapon Quality","pct":98},{"name":"Swimming","pct":98},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":98}]', 'Skills of note only. Climbing is printed 98%/98$ and Horsemanship: Exotic Animals 98%/98%; the first figure is kept. Gymnastics is printed with no percentage. Printed as Literacy: Dragonese/Elf, Math: Basic, Play Musical Instrument: String/Guitar and Pilot Hover Craft (Ground); those carry their catalog names. Literacy: American has no catalog row. Paired Weapons is the catalog''s W.P. Paired Weapons.', 'Has all that any Beast has and more: P.S. and P.E. both Supernatural, flight on wings at any altitude including outer space, needs no air, no harm from ordinary cold and half from magic cold, half damage from fire, nightvision 120 feet (36.6 m), sees the invisible, Dimensional Teleport 92%, knows all languages by magic at 92%, Bio-Regenerates 4D6 M.D.C. once a melee round and regrows a lost limb or horn in 96 hours. Shifts at will into a plain mortal man or woman, or into a red-brown bull half again the size of the biggest natural one, which triples his running Spd. Metal Behemoth, a gift of Lady Hel: in any of his forms he can turn his body to steel, gaining 800 M.D.C. and strength. Summon Deevils, also her gift: once a day he calls 1D6 Deevils or a single Beast to serve him. Vulnerabilities: those of every Beast; in steel his speed halves and he can cast no spell until he turns back to flesh; Rune and Holy Weapons do him double damage in either state. His longing for Lady Hel could make him quit the war or turn on Sahtalus if she spurns him, and he badly underrates humans and other mortals and never learns from losing to them.', 'All spells of levels 1-4, plus Agony (20), Animate and Control Dead (20), Armor Bizarre (15), Ballistic Fire (25), Banishment (65), Blight of Ages (600), Call Lightning (15), Calling (8), Circle of Flame (10), Death Curse (Special), Desiccate the Supernatural (50), Domination (10), Energy Disruption (12), Escape (8), Fire Ball (10), Fire Blossom (20), Heal Wounds (10), Life Drain (25), Lightblade (20), Lightning Arc (30), Minor Curse (35), Negate Magic (30), Power Bolt (20), Realm of Chaos (70), Spinning Blades (20), Steel Rain (360), Sub-Particle Acceleration (20), Vicious Circle (350) and Wind Rush (20). P.P.E. 422. None while in his steel form. Animate and Control Dead is printed as Animate & Control Dead.', 'None.', NULL, NULL, 'Deceiver, a Rune battle axe (catalog gear row deceiver): 6D6 M.D. in each of its three shapes (for him an axe, a pole arm and a spear), changing shape costs one melee action, and a foe who fails a save vs magic of 14 is -2 to parry or dodge it. It has the eight Rune Weapon traits, is Miscreant, drinks souls, can pass as any stringed instrument, and casts Aura of Power, Multiple Image, Horrific Illusion and Horror three times a day each. As a battle axe its haft is an electric guitar, which he has learned to play. He wears no armor: he turns to steel instead.', 'Treasure said to be worth over 100 million credits, hidden away; some worlds worship him as a god.', 'Cocky and arrogant, he expects perfection of himself and his soldiers and asks nothing of them he would not do himself, so he leads from the front line. Bold but never reckless, his gambles are reckoned ones. He rarely admits a mistake, treats a tactical withdrawal as a small setback caused by one overlooked factor, and always comes back for a rematch. He keeps grudges forever and remembers the face of anyone who ever bested him, and he always underrates humans.', 'Lady Hel, wife of Sahtalus, is his chief patron; his fondness for her is sliding into delusion. He cares little for the Minion War itself and fights it for her sake.', 'Deevils in his own ranks who once served Regent Grizza, whom he killed: they had easier posts under Grizza, resent him, and know of his longing for Lady Hel and mean to use it. He has an old rivalry with Overlord Shard, the two forever chasing the same prize, now the conquest of Rifts Earth; Sindel has heard Shard is a coward and a madman and means to beat him to it.', 'A Deevil Beast whose rise began before the Minion War, when he led an elite force of 10,000 minions and armies of mortals taken from the worlds he conquered for Dyval. Called home to defend Dyval under the lazy, inept Regent Grizza, he did his best, then followed Grizza into the Tower Grim and killed him in front of Sahtalus and the Deevil Lords. Lady Hel spoke for him, crediting him with driving the demons back, and the Lords made him an Overlord. He has served her since; she gave him the steel form and the power to summon Deevils, and he courts her openly, with rumors that he plans first to conquer Rifts Earth, then to contest Sahtalus for her and the throne. His army, the Steel Bloods, under a silver banner showing a black fist dripping blood, is among the most brutal on the Deevil side: it takes no prisoners it cannot enslave, sacrifice or eat, uses whatever weapons it finds (Blood and Bone weapons are favoured, some commanders ride Walking Deaths and he rides a young Flying Horror), and aims at the Canadian Southeast, meaning to take Iron Heart, Free Quebec and Lazlo and raise two Hell Pits inside a captured city. He may turn on the Xiticix first, which would cost him half his host.', 'Rifts World Book 35: Megaverse in Flames p.165-168'),
('overlord-sthena', 'Overlord Sthena', 'Ning Manna''Bri (true name)', 'Deevil Overlord of the Royal Medusa, leader of the Vipers army', 'rifts', 'Royal Medusa (Gorgon of Dyval)', '12th level; no O.C.C. is printed (as printed)', 12, 'Aberrant', 'Effectively Immortal', '6 feet (1.8 m) in her humanoid form; 11 feet (3.3 m) as a Medusa Gorgon', '180 pounds (81 kg) in her humanoid form; 1,200 pounds (540 kg) as a Medusa Gorgon', '{"IQ":21,"ME":20,"MA":25,"PS":31,"PP":24,"PE":22,"PB":26,"Spd":20}', 220, 400, 800, 322, NULL, 13, 17, '{"attacks":8,"initiative":4,"strike":8,"parry":8,"dodge":8,"pull":3,"roll":3}', 'Horror Factor 17 in her Medusa form only. Hit Points 220, S.D.C. 400 and A.R. 13 are the block''s S.D.C.-setting figures (that line prints her name as Stheno). Also +6 on Perception Rolls and cannot be surprised from behind in Medusa form, +8 to save vs Horror Factor, +6 vs magic, +7 vs psionics and +2 on spell strength. Her snakes add 1D6+1 minor attacks a melee round beyond her eight. Supernatural P.S. 31. W.P. Archery and W.P. Chain.', '[{"name":"Barter","pct":82},{"name":"Brewing","pct":88},{"name":"Climbing","pct":98},{"name":"Concealment","pct":72},{"name":"Dance","pct":93},{"name":"Disguise","pct":88},{"name":"Holistic Medicine","pct":93},{"name":"Impersonation","pct":82},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":88},{"name":"Literacy: Dragonese/Elven","pct":93},{"name":"Literacy: Demongogian","pct":93},{"name":"Literacy: American","pct":93},{"name":"Literacy: Greek","pct":93},{"name":"Lore: Demons & Monsters","pct":88},{"name":"Mathematics: Basic","pct":98},{"name":"Mythology","pct":93},{"name":"Palming","pct":83},{"name":"Performance","pct":93},{"name":"Prowl","pct":88},{"name":"Seduction","pct":76},{"name":"Sing","pct":98},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":72},{"name":"Swimming","pct":98},{"name":"Tracking (people)","pct":88}]', 'Skills of note only. Brewing is printed 88%/93%, Climbing 98%/93%, Holistic Medicine 93%/83% and Impersonation 82%/68%; the first figure is kept. Printed as Literacy: Dragonese and Lore: Demons and Monsters; those carry their catalog names, Literacy: Dragonese/Elven and Lore: Demons & Monsters. Literacy: Demongogian, American and Greek have no catalog row.', 'Every ability of the Gorgons of Dyval, among them a 900 foot (274 m) range of nightvision, sees the invisible and the infrared, changes size, keen sight and cannot be surprised while her hair is a mass of snakes, Dimensional Teleport 76%, half damage from fire and cold, Bio-Regenerates 3D6 M.D.C. a melee round, speaks and understands every language by magic, and has the Gorgon''s petrifying gaze. Metamorphosis: Human, into one form only, herself with hair instead of serpents; the change takes half a melee (7 seconds) and lasts as long as she likes, as often as she likes. Her 5D6+20 snakes reach six feet (1.8 m), give her 1D6+1 extra bite attacks a melee round, can parry (+2), entangle and hold a foe or snatch a weapon (+1 to disarm), have 1D6 M.D.C. each and regrow in 24 hours if killed or severed. Vulnerabilities: those of the Gorgon; ordinary bone or silver weapons do their S.D.C. damage to her as M.D.; weapons that do extra damage to serpents or Deevils work on her, and holy weapons and dragon-bone weapons do double damage.', 'All invocations of levels 1-3, plus Animate and Control Dead (20), Blind (6), Carpet of Adhesion (10), Call Lightning (15), Constrain Being (20), Deflect (10), Desiccate the Supernatural (50), Energy Sphere (120), Eyes of Thoth (8), Exorcism (30), Magic Net (7), Mask of Deceit (15), Mystic Portal (60), Negate Magic (30), Remove Curse (140), Spoil (30), Stone to Flesh (30) and Teleport: Superior (600). P.P.E. 322. Animate and Control Dead is printed as Animate & Control Dead.', 'None.', NULL, NULL, 'Red and gold plate and chain armor of 300 M.D.C. that makes her impervious to fire (half damage from magic fire) and regenerates 1D10 M.D.C. an hour. A one-of-a-kind longbow of a blue-purple exotic metal strung with a supple magic chain, firing at up to 3,000 feet (914.4 m): bone arrows (4D6 M.D.), Deevil arrows or any magic arrow. She carries a dozen of every arrow in this book, plus Eternally Sharp arrows (+3 to damage), Demon Slayer arrows (double damage to demons) and modern explosive-tipped arrows. The bow splits into a spiked flail joined by its chain, with an 8 foot (2.4 m) reach, doing 3D6+3 M.D. and able to strike with Numbing Cold three times a day (save 13 or more; a victim loses two melee attacks and is -2 to strike, parry, dodge and the like for 1D6 melee rounds).', 'Gems and magic items worth 25 million credits in a vault at Center on Phase World, her fallback; on Rifts Earth she has quickly gathered 2.5 million Universal Credits and one million credits in Black Market goods.', 'A master of seduction, guile and murder, with long dark hair that shows red in the right light and almond-shaped emerald-green eyes. She will play any part, helpless innocent included, to win a foe''s trust. Beneath it she is driven, focused and venomous, ready to lie, steal, cheat and kill for her goals, merciless to demons and caring little for anyone but Medusa and Gorgons. Yet she admires real heroes, mortals too, for courage, character, kindness and mercy, and sometimes quietly lets one escape, or grants a quick and painless death instead.', 'The Royal Medusa who broke out of exile with her, fanatically loyal, serve as her bodyguards, spies and assassins. Mephisto courts her favour, but she will deal only with Sahtalus. The Gorgons respect and fear her and obey her as an Overlord, though they resent the Medusa''s airs and would not mourn her. In Europe she has allied with the Angel of Death and her Brodkil Empire.', 'Demons first. She and Lady Leviathan loathe each other, which earns her no friends among Leviathan''s followers, Queen Marauder''s army above all; she expects to clash with Marauder and would enjoy humbling one of Leviathan''s factions, so long as it does not endanger the Deevils'' war on the demons.', 'Leader of the Royal Medusa, Gorgons who can pass as lovely human women and use the guise to infiltrate, seduce and kill. The tale goes that Lady Leviathan, jealous of their beauty, banished them to a bleak prison dimension; Sthena claims to be one of the first of them, and after the Medusa broke free together she asked Sahtalus to restore them to Dyval''s pantheon and send her to Rifts Earth as an Overlord to prove their worth. Lady Hel, to spite Leviathan, persuaded him, so Sthena answers to no Deevil Lord but is provisionally under the House of Sahtalus, with 3,000 Medusa still held in exile as surety; she wants their release, revenge on Leviathan and one day a Lord''s seat of her own. Her army, the Vipers, disciplined and organised, flies a purple flag with a golden cobra. It entered Europe through the Tree of Darkness, which shut the portal before even a quarter of her forces crossed, and with Queen Marauder ahead of her at the Gargoyle Empire she joined the Angel of Death, quietly raising Brodkil, rogue Gargoyles and Gurgoyles to wear down both the demons and Marauder, leave the NGR alone for now, and later take Poland, France, the NGR and the Sovietski.', 'Rifts World Book 35: Megaverse in Flames p.169-171'),
('queen-marauder', 'Queen Marauder', 'Phi''Nth Jot''Pol (true name)', 'Self-styled Queen of all Dire Harpies, soon to be Overlord, leader of the Flying Marauders army', 'rifts', 'Dire Harpy merged with a Greater Fire Elemental (an experiment of the Deevil Lord Leviathan)', '8th level; no O.C.C. is printed (as printed)', 8, 'Miscreant', 'Effectively Immortal', 'Changes at will from 6 feet to 18 feet (1.8 to 5.5 m)', '800 pounds (360 kg)', '{"IQ":15,"ME":22,"MA":18,"PS":26,"PP":22,"PE":20,"PB":22,"Spd":20}', 224, 160, 428, 420, NULL, 13, 14, '{"attacks":7,"initiative":3,"strike":6,"parry":5,"dodge":5,"disarm":2,"pull":4,"roll":4}', 'Spd 20 on foot and 110 flying (75 mph/120 km). Hit Points 224, S.D.C. 160 and A.R. 13 are the block''s S.D.C.-setting figures. +8 to dodge when flying. Also +6 to save vs Horror Factor, +4 vs magic and +6 vs psionics. Her shield adds +1 to parry and disarm. Supernatural P.S. 26. W.P. Blunt, W.P. Energy Pistol, W.P. Spear and W.P. Shield.', '[{"name":"Appraise Goods","pct":75},{"name":"Astronomy & Navigation","pct":75},{"name":"Barter","pct":78},{"name":"Climbing","pct":84},{"name":"Dance","pct":85},{"name":"Detect Ambush","pct":75},{"name":"Gemology","pct":70},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":80},{"name":"Horsemanship: Exotic Animals","pct":85},{"name":"Lore: Demons & Monsters","pct":80},{"name":"Lore: Faeries & Creatures of Magic","pct":80},{"name":"Mathematics: Basic","pct":98},{"name":"Military Etiquette","pct":89},{"name":"Prowl","pct":80},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":80},{"name":"Surveillance","pct":85},{"name":"Tracking (people)","pct":84},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":98}]', 'Skills of note only. Climbing is printed as Climb 84%/74% and Horsemanship: Exotic Animals 85%/75%; the first figure is kept.', 'Flies at any altitude, outer space included, and glides; nightvision 900 feet (274.3 m); sees the invisible; Bio-Regenerates 3D6 M.D. a melee round; twice a day summons 3D6 Harpies or 2D4 Dire Harpies; fire, magic fire included, does her no harm; speaks and understands every language by magic and can talk with Fire Elementals; Teleport 60% to as far as 5 miles (8 km) at will, plus a 30% Dimensional Teleport. She can Expel Fire Bolts from her eyes or hands at will (see attacks). Fiery Aura: for 30 P.P.E. a sheath of flame gives her 200 more M.D.C. for 10 minutes or until spent, and burns anyone who touches her who is not fireproof. Fiery Meteor Strike, once a day: she becomes a streaking fireball at triple flying speed and slams one target (+3 to strike), spending six of her next melee attacks; for 1D4 melee rounds afterward she has three attacks a melee and half her Spd and combat bonuses. Vulnerabilities: cold and water attacks do double damage, a gallon (3.78 liters) of water burns her for 4D6 M.D. so she shelters from rain, and Holy Weapons do double damage.', 'All Fire Elemental magic of levels 1-6, plus Fire Blossom (20), Fire Globe (40), Fire Gout (20) and Firequake (160). P.P.E. 420.', 'None.', NULL, NULL, 'Enchanted golden plate and chain armor of 150 M.D.C., impervious to fire, weightless and silent. A shield of 200 M.D.C. adding +1 to parry and disarm. The Spear of Fire, a Lesser Rune weapon with the standard traits that returns when thrown, does 4D6 M.D. and three times a day becomes a flaming missile (see attacks).', 'Valuables worth over 30 million credits taken in her conquests.', 'Cunning, sly and playful, she toys with prey like a cat with a mouse, letting captives think they are about to escape before shutting the door on them. Against an army she probes its defences again and again for a weak spot, then exploits it without mercy, and she is a master of feints and false weakness that draw a foe into ambush, a ploy that works especially well against the rash demons of Hades. Once battle is joined she holds nothing back. Beautiful herself, she still shares the Harpies'' envy of beauty and loves to maim, enslave and destroy lovely things and people.', 'Harpies and Dire Harpies, who revere her as a shaman or a figure of authority, and the Deevil troops she commands. For now she reports directly to Leviathan.', 'The demons of Hades above all, and Night Owls, which she hunts down whenever she can. Overlord Sthena is her rival by default, and Leviathan may use Marauder to be rid of that upstart. Mortals are toys and subjects to be conquered and enslaved.', 'Leviathan tried to strengthen her Harpies by fusing them with Fire Elemental magic; every attempt failed until one Dire Harpy merged with a Greater Fire Elemental became an angel-like woman with sun-coloured feathered wings and eyes of fire. Harpies flocked to her at once and hailed her as their queen, and almost none of them know where she came from. Jealous, Leviathan meant to destroy her, but Marauder asked to prove herself in the Minion War, and Leviathan, before thousands of her Harpies, agreed on condition that she win her first hundred battles in Leviathan''s name or die slowly, flayed and plucked. She has won 99; one more makes her Overlord Marauder and a strong candidate to become Deevil Lord of Rifts Earth. Her army, the Flying Marauders, flies a red and blue square flag bearing a gold shield pierced by a spear. It leans on Harpy and Dire Harpy air cavalry, with smaller ground forces that ride Hell Schooners and Hell Battle Barges and carry Kreelo''s Blood Energy and Hell weapons, with about 20 each of Meat Grinders and Carnage tanks. Massed outside the Gargoyle Empire in Germany, she hopes to ally with the rogue Gargoyles against the NGR in exchange for the region''s ley line nexus points, a plan the arriving demons have turned into a free-for-all, while part of her force digs a Hell Pit in the Black Forest; Poland is to follow the NGR.', 'Rifts World Book 35: Megaverse in Flames p.172-173');
